id: hyped
name: Hyped
kind: conditions
maxStacks: 1
# Not a Combat Condition: the entry says "you become Hyped!" and never calls it one.
combatCondition: no
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Carried by your own performance. Every Combat Roll gains 1(T) plus a quarter of
  your Personality Modifier, rounded up.
text: >
  Hyped: the Hype Maneuver's mark. "You become Hyped! While Hyped, increase your
  Combat Rolls by 1(T)+1/4 (rounded up) of your Personality Modifier until the end
  of your next turn."

---

# Not a Combat Condition the rulebook lists, and the entry that creates it does not
# call it one - "you become Hyped!", where Called Shot's examples say "gains the
# Impediment Combat Condition". It is kept here for the reason Analyzed is: this is
# where a mark on a character with a clock on it lives.
#
# Unlike Analyzed, this one carries its own rule. "Increase YOUR Combat Rolls" is
# about whoever is Hyped and nobody else, and a passive is exactly a rule about
# whoever is holding it - so it goes here rather than in the Maneuver, and anything
# else that ever makes somebody Hyped gets the same bonus without being told.
#
# `combatRolls` is the rulebook's own term for the three - the Strike, the Dodge and
# the Wound Roll - and the Slot fans out to all three, so this is one line rather than
# three.
[passive]
combatRolls += 1(T) + ceil(personality.mod / 4);
